`pmap` – Shows the memory layout of a running process.
`PID` – Unique process identification number.
`pmap PID` – Displays memory mapping details of a given process.
`pmap -x PID` – Provides extended memory usage information for a process.
`top` – Monitors active processes and their resource consumption.
`ps` – Displays details of currently running processes.
`ps aux` – Lists all processes with detailed information.
`grep` – Searches for a particular process or text.
`&` – Executes a program in the background.
`kill` – Sends a signal to terminate a process.
`Address` – Represents the starting location of a memory region.
`Kbytes` – Indicates memory size in kilobytes.
`RSS` – Shows the physical RAM occupied by a process.
`Dirty` – Represents modified memory pages that may need to be written to storage.
`total` – Shows the combined memory usage of the process.
